  "scope": "C399 scalar64-bit private table cells, numeric LOW32 full arena index/HIGH32 original rejection fingerprint. Same8B per slot (uint64 alignment8 vs struct4, ordinary actual allocators align both), original low32 hash home/probe/load threshold/doubling/arena/index/countrybits/fullkey equality. Snapshot cell supplies index directly; fingerprint shifted only after occupied check. Grow extracts the same fingerprint and copies whole cells; index0 alone empty, hash0/1/MAX legal. Original end-of-loop index reload retained, no rejected305 pointer carry, cache/hint/grouping/sharedtable/bitwidth/domain/queue/parser/role/default/ISA/PGO change. One explicit allocation-exception hardening: own uninitialized slab in unique_ptr before storage-vector push; no zero-fill pass/capacity change. Compiler may still split/reshape loads; no guaranteed single-load/uop/Intel benefit. Existing original GNU static code has two field reads, but is not a frequency/performance or new-code proof. Need fresh actual-header numeric encode/decode/allindex/0/1/MAX/empty/grow/collision/fullkey/guard/arena/fault/country/privateowner models, main strict/race/untrained/GNU/image/default/Make/real proof if promising. No old struct/group4 correctness or native gain transferred.",
